<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Locarno Treaties</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1925</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Locarno Pact</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/locarno">Locarno</a> Treaties were agreements negotiated at Locarno in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> in October 1925 and signed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> that December. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a> accepted their common borders, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> as guarantors, and Germany agreed arbitration with its eastern neighbours. The treaties eased post-war tensions and led to Germany's entry into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a> in 1926.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/locarno-treaties.jpg" alt="Locarno Treaties" width="320" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UnknownUnknown · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-R03618,_Locarno,_Gustav_Stresemann,_Chamberlain,_Briand.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
